<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    ============================================================
    bg_brand_dot — circular brand-accent dot
    ------------------------------------------------------------
    A simple oval filled with ?attr/colorPrimary.

    Why a theme attribute and not a fixed color resource:
      - @color/pulse_accent would be correct in the current
        Phase-1 placeholder screen, but would break the moment
        the dot is reused on a dark surface where the accent
        indigo (#6D5EF5) reads as too heavy.
      - ?attr/colorPrimary resolves through the active theme:
        #6D5EF5 (md_primary_light) on light, #9A91FF
        (md_primary_dark) on dark. Same file, both themes,
        correct color in each.

    Why <shape android:shape="oval">:
      - The parent View in activity_main.xml has fixed
        width=height=12dp. An oval shape in a square bounds
        renders as a perfect circle. If the width and height
        were unequal (say 12dp × 20dp), the oval would render
        as an ellipse — for pills we would use
        <corners android:radius="50dp"> on a rectangle
        instead. Keep this drawable consumed only by square
        bounds; anything non-square should use a separate
        drawable with a pill shape.

    No stroke, no padding, no gradient:
      - Adding a stroke would produce a ring, not a dot.
        The dot is meant to read as a single colored element.
      - A gradient at 12dp is invisible on most screens and
        adds render cost for zero visual benefit — solid color
        is the correct choice at this size.
    ============================================================
-->
<shape
    xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="oval">

    <solid android:color="?attr/colorPrimary" />

</shape>
